/*
 * The +50 "First Finisher" treasure bonus paid as +100 instead, written as the
 * presence of a file: custom_mods\first_finisher_100_on under the game folder,
 * beside Rance10.exe. Delete it and the bonus goes back to +50. It is read as
 * the battle result is calculated, so neither direction takes a restart.
 *
 * This is the switch half of the feature; the hook that reaches the bonus is
 * first_finisher_100.jam next door, and feature.js in this folder names the
 * pair. What each file is and why it is the kind of file it is is said there.
 *
 * WHAT +100 BUYS. The chest after a won battle is one RAND(100) <= total, where
 * total is a plain sum of five bonuses and 100 or more is a guaranteed chest --
 * docs/treasure-chest-chance.md has the arithmetic. The First Finisher line is
 * one of the five and ships worth 50. At 100 it clears the threshold on its own,
 * so a battle that pays it is a certain chest whatever the other four add. On
 * its own this feature therefore makes the first kill of each character a sure
 * chest, once per quest; paired with always-first-finisher, which pays the line
 * on every won battle rather than the first kill, it is a sure chest every won
 * battle. The two are the "always" and the "full" of the same bonus.
 *
 * WHY A HELPER RATHER THAN THE WHOLE OVERRIDE HERE. The figure lives as the
 * `value` argument to BattleBonusCollection@Set#1, whose first parameter is the
 * enum BattleBonusType. alice-tools' .jaf compiler will not name that enum -- a
 * `BattleBonusType type` parameter is a parse error and an `int type` one is a
 * type error the moment super() is handed it back (expected enum#92; got int).
 * So the substitution is assembled in the .jam, which has no type system in the
 * way, and this file is only the part that is cleaner as source: the switch-file
 * check. The .jam calls it with the shipped value as the fallback, so anything
 * but the switched-on First Finisher gets its own number back and an .ain with
 * this feature in it and no switch file behaves exactly as an unpatched one.
 *
 * The path is spelled with forward slashes because the .jaf lexer does not take
 * a backslash in a string literal at all, and Windows accepts either separator.
 * It is looked for twice for the reason features/reliable-cooking/
 * cooking_skill_chance.jaf gives: whether SystemService.GetGameFolderPath() ends
 * in a separator is something the game does not agree with itself about, and
 * trying both spellings settles it without running the game. A path that does
 * not resolve reads as "no file", which is the harmless direction -- the shipped
 * +50.
 */
int FirstFinisher100Value(int fallback)
{
	string folder = SystemService.GetGameFolderPath();
	if (FileOperation.ExistFile(folder + "custom_mods/first_finisher_100_on")
	 || FileOperation.ExistFile(folder + "/custom_mods/first_finisher_100_on")) {
		return 100;
	}
	return fallback;
}
